  era: "c. 1300 \xB7 Section 14 \xB7 Delhi Sultanate \xB7 1206 \u2013 1526"
  title: Sultanate military
  text: The sultans kept a large standing army of cavalry, with horses imported from Central Asia and Arabia, and war elephants. Alauddin Khalji introduced the branding of horses, called dagh, and descriptive rolls of soldiers, called huliya.
